      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(telegram): reject malformed table spans",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Telegram rich-block table rendering could treat malformed HTML table span attributes as valid numbers when assistant-authored HTML contained values like `colspan=\"2x\"` or `rowspan=\"3y\"`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nTelegram table span parsing now accepts only complete decimal integer span values and keeps malformed spans as ordinary one-cell table entries. The legacy HTML table fallback also requires a real `colspan` attribute boundary so unrelated attributes such as `data-colspan` cannot hide a later valid span.\n\nRelated independent bug-family PRs: this is part of a strict external numeric-token parsing wave; each PR is independent, based on `upstream/main`, and has no merge dependency on the others.\n\n## User Impact\n\nTelegram users get table output that matches authored spans more predictably instead of silently expanding malformed partial values into wider or taller cells.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Current head: `601074457c99bebb9fb4931fea299da87489c6d4`.\n- Native Telegram Desktop proof: Mantis run https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29579183461 passed and published before/after artifacts showing malformed `colspan` stays a normal one-cell table entry in this PR while the baseline renders an extra blank table column.\n- Artifact bundle: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29579183461/artifacts/8407192096\n- Focused regression coverage for this span parser change remains limited to `extensions/telegram/src/rich-blocks-html.test.ts` and `extensions/telegram/src/format.test.ts`; current branch diff is the same four Telegram parser/test files after rebasing onto `e7f4b993943735373f93e9d719d0b9e4ca6e37b1`.",
